cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Parley"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Natheeswaran
    given-names: Parusan
    alias: Parusann
repository-code: "https://github.com/Parusann/parley"
url: "https://github.com/Parusann/parley"
abstract: >-
  Parley is a free, fully offline, push-to-talk voice dictation tool for
  Windows. It uses OpenAI Whisper (via faster-whisper or a GPU-accelerated
  whisper.cpp Vulkan server) to transcribe speech to text at the cursor, with
  global hotkeys, voice commands, vocabulary correction, per-app rules, and
  optional local LLM polish via Ollama. No audio or transcript data leaves
  the user's machine. Parley builds on drajb/whisper-local and its parent
  PinW/whisper-key-local.
keywords:
  - speech-to-text
  - dictation
  - whisper
  - voice-typing
  - transcription
  - privacy
  - offline
  - local-ai
  - accessibility
license: MIT
